# NgRx Toolkit Usage Rules

## Source Attribution
**Source**: [Context7 - Angular Architects NgRx Toolkit](https://context7.com/angular-architects/ngrx-toolkit)
**Purpose**: Comprehensive NgRx usage guidelines and best practices

## NgRx Store Fundamentals

### 1. Store Setup and Structure
```typescript
// ✅ Feature state interface
export interface UserState {
  users: User[];
  selectedUser: User | null;
  loading: boolean;
  error: string | null;
}

// ✅ Root state
export interface AppState {
  user: UserState;
  products: ProductState;
}

// ✅ Feature module registration
StoreModule.forFeature('user', userReducer),
EffectsModule.forFeature([UserEffects]),
```

### 2. Actions and Action Creators
```typescript
// ✅ Action creators
import { createAction, props } from '@ngrx/store';

export const loadUsers = createAction('[User] Load Users');
export const loadUsersSuccess = createAction('[User] Load Users Success', props<{ users: User[] }>());
export const loadUsersFailure = createAction('[User] Load Users Failure', props<{ error: string }>());
```

### 3. Reducers and State Updates
```typescript
// ✅ Reducer with immer for immutable updates
import { createReducer, on } from '@ngrx/store';
import { loadUsers, loadUsersSuccess, loadUsersFailure } from './user.actions';

export const initialState: UserState = {
  users: [],
  selectedUser: null,
  loading: false,
  error: null
};

export const userReducer = createReducer(
  initialState,
  on(loadUsers, state => ({ ...state, loading: true, error: null })),
  on(loadUsersSuccess, (state, { users }) => ({ ...state, users, loading: false })),
  on(loadUsersFailure, (state, { error }) => ({ ...state, error, loading: false }))
);
```

### 4. Selectors
```typescript
// ✅ Selectors
import { createSelector, createFeatureSelector } from '@ngrx/store';

export const selectUserState = createFeatureSelector<AppState, UserState>('user');

export const selectAllUsers = createSelector(
  selectUserState,
  (state: UserState) => state.users
);

export const selectSelectedUser = createSelector(
  selectUserState,
  (state: UserState) => state.selectedUser
);
```

### 5. Effects
```typescript
// ✅ Effects for side effects
import { Actions, createEffect, ofType } from '@ngrx/effects';
import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';
import { UserService } from '../services/user.service';
import { loadUsers, loadUsersSuccess, loadUsersFailure } from './user.actions';
import { catchError, map, mergeMap, of } from 'rxjs';

@Injectable()
export class UserEffects {
  loadUsers$ = createEffect(() => this.actions$.pipe(
    ofType(loadUsers),
    mergeMap(() => this.userService.getUsers().pipe(
      map(users => loadUsersSuccess({ users })),
      catchError(error => of(loadUsersFailure({ error: error.message })))
    ))
  ));

  constructor(
    private actions$: Actions,
    private userService: UserService
  ) {}
}
```

### 6. Entity Adapter
```typescript
// ✅ Entity adapter for normalized state
import { createEntityAdapter, EntityState } from '@ngrx/entity';

export interface UserEntityState extends EntityState<User> {
  selectedUserId: number | null;
}

export const userAdapter = createEntityAdapter<User>();

export const initialState: UserEntityState = userAdapter.getInitialState({
  selectedUserId: null
});

export const userReducer = createReducer(
  initialState,
  on(loadUsersSuccess, (state, { users }) => userAdapter.setAll(users, state)),
  // ... other handlers
);
```

### 7. Best Practices
- Use feature modules for state separation
- Use action creators and props for type safety
- Use selectors for state querying
- Use effects for side effects and async operations
- Use entity adapter for normalized state
- Avoid business logic in reducers and effects
- Use OnPush change detection in components
- Use the async pipe for store observables
- Implement proper error handling in effects
- Write unit tests for reducers, selectors, and effects

### 8. Testing
```typescript
// ✅ Testing reducers
describe('UserReducer', () => {
  it('should set loading true on loadUsers', () => {
    const action = loadUsers();
    const state = userReducer(initialState, action);
    expect(state.loading).toBeTrue();
  });
});

// ✅ Testing selectors
describe('UserSelectors', () => {
  it('should select all users', () => {
    const state: AppState = {
      user: {
        users: [{ id: 1, name: 'John' }],
        selectedUser: null,
        loading: false,
        error: null
      },
      products: { /* ... */ }
    };
    expect(selectAllUsers(state)).toEqual([{ id: 1, name: 'John' }]);
  });
});
```

## Best Practices Summary

### Do's ✅
- Use feature modules for state
- Use action creators and props
- Use selectors for querying state
- Use effects for side effects
- Use entity adapter for normalized state
- Use OnPush change detection
- Use async pipe in components
- Write unit tests for store logic

### Don'ts ❌
- Put business logic in reducers/effects
- Mutate state directly
- Use manual subscriptions in components
- Ignore error handling
- Skip testing
- Overcomplicate state structure
- Mix feature and global state

This comprehensive guide ensures proper NgRx usage following best practices and Angular Architects recommendations.
